US Census government boundaries, BAS 2026

Source: U.S. Census Bureau, TIGERweb Places and County Subdivisions,
January 1, BAS 2026 vintage. Captured 2026-11-04.
https://tigerweb.geo.census.gov/arcgis/rest/services/TIGERweb/Places_CouSub_ConCity_SubMCD/MapServer
Layer 8: County Subdivisions; layer 11: Incorporated Places.
Only FUNCSTAT=A: active government providing primary general-purpose functions.
https://www.census.gov/library/reference/code-lists/functional-status-codes.html
State FIPS/postal abbreviations:
https://www2.census.gov/geo/docs/reference/state.txt

Public domain, a work of the United States government (17 USC 105).
The Census Bureau requests source citation. No Census endorsement is implied.
https://www2.census.gov/geo/pdfs/maps-data/data/tiger/tgrshp2026/TGRSHP2026_TechDoc_Ch1.pdf

Modified: retained source-namespace/GEOID, state, NAME and full-resolution
polygon rings, requested WGS84 output (outSR=4326), rounded coordinates to
1e-7 degrees and delta-encoded each ring. No geometric simplification.
The 35,703 captured active-government entities were checked for completeness
and duplicate IDs. Omitted 1,072 invalid geometries and then 91 valid records
outside the 50 states/DC. Retained 34,540 entities in 44,208 polygon parts.
The pinned gzip SHA256 is
fff1d0c08c837671318e57ec148719c2c98776f481fc40e9939cf087e8b78f75.

Census boundaries are statistical representations, not legal land descriptions
or a determination of jurisdictional authority or property ownership. Census
provides no positional-accuracy warranty; output precision is not surveyed
accuracy. The coordinate-encoding boundary guard does not bound source error.
This source excludes statistical CDPs, nonfunctioning entities and government
statuses other than A. It does not establish postal-city or community identity.
